@media
title: Dossier IV — Media, movements and institutional memory
new-page: true

= What outlives the campaign

Editorial independence finishes at **[+ media_editorial_independence +]**,
distribution resilience at **[+ media_distribution_resilience +]**, legal
security at **[+ media_legal_security +]** and safety capacity at **[+
media_safety_capacity +]**. Election-information integrity is **[+
election_information_integrity +]**.

The media star recorded by the campaign is **[+ media_star_name +]**. The
deepfake source remains **[+ media_deepfake_source +]**. [? if
media_parallel_done: Election-night parallel realities changed trust and
reception, never the certified vote or seats.?]

Black Monday, Black Friday and the 2019 teachers' strike remain fixed
pre-campaign history. Their movement autonomy, repression and union memories
survive as starting conditions and legacies, not retroactive flashbacks.

